MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-10 Start Cutscene
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: 'In Madrid, a number of young Filipinos were intense enthusiasts over
      political agitation, and with the carelessness of the youth, were careless
      of what they said or how they said it. A sort of social club had been organized
      by older Filipinos and Spaniards interested in the Philippines, with the idea
      of quietly assisting toward improved insular conditions, but it became so radical
      under the influence of this younger majority, that its conservative members
      were compelled to drop out and the club broke up. '
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: At first the project was severely criticised; later a few conformed
      to the plan, and Rizal believed that his scheme was in a fair way of accomplishment.
      At the meeting to discuss the details, however, each member of the company
      wanted to write about the Filipino woman, and the rest of the subjects scarcely
      interested any of them. I was disgusted with this trifling and dropped the
      affair, nor did I ever again seem to take any very enthusiastic interest in
      such popular movements.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: In my stay in Madrid, I have come across a second-hand copy, in two
      volumes, of a French novel, which I bought to improve my knowledge of that
      language. One may disagree or agree with its teachings and concede or dispute
      its literary merits, it cannot be denied that it was the most powerful book
      in its effects on the century. The book that I wrote in my diary affected me
      powerfully, with a tremendous sympathy for the unfortunates that made me willing
      to risk everything on their behalf.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Stories which I could get from my companions were written down and
      revised, until finally the half had been prepared of what was finally the novel.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: In 1884, I had begun my studies in English; I had been studying French
      during and since my voyage to Spain; Italian was acquired apparently at a time
      when the exposition of Genoa had attracted Spanish interest toward Italy, and
      largely through the reading of Italian translations of works which he knew
      in other languages
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: German, too, I had started to study, but had not advanced far with
      it. Thus I was then preparing myself for the travels through Europe which I
      had intended to make from the time when I first left my home, for I well knew
      that it was only by knowing the language of a country that it would be possible
      for me to study the people, see in what way they differed from his own, and
      find out which of their customs and what lessons from their history might be
      of advantage to the Filipinos.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
